.jekyll-cache

# Gemfile.lock stays untracked ON PURPOSE.
#
# It used to be committed, and that broke the deployed site: the lock was
# generated on local Ruby 2.6 / Bundler 1.17, while CI runs Ruby 3.1 (Bundler
# 2.x). Under that mismatched lock the CI build silently produced zero-byte
# HTML pages and an empty _posts collection. Do not commit it back unless the
# whole toolchain is pinned to one environment, including a .ruby-version file.
/Gemfile.lock

# ide
.claude

# macOS / editor droppings, at any depth.
**/.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Local-only helper scripts.
*.sh
!apush.sh

